     1	# Ownership decision table — install/upgrade conditional surfaces
     2	
     3	> **Status:** W0 product of PLAN-167. The enum in §3 is a *draft* until the
     4	> PLAN-167 W1 debate ratifies or amends it. The open questions in §6 are
     5	> deliberately unresolved here — they are the debate's agenda.
     6	>
     7	> **Two known inconsistencies are committed on purpose.** Writing the decision
     8	> function against this table (the W2 proposal) exposed them, and resolving
     9	> them unilaterally would pre-decide exactly what the debate exists to settle:
    10	>
    11	> 1. **The table is not self-consistent about `OMIT_RECORD`.** Some rows with a
    12	>    prior record expect `OMIT_RECORD`, others with a prior record expect
    13	>    `PRESERVE_UNOWNED`. Sixty-one hand-written rows never had to agree with
    14	>    each other; a function has to. See OQ-9.
    15	> 2. **`OWN-0018` and `OWN-0020` have identical dimensions and opposite
    16	>    outcomes**, separated only by a prose directive in `note`. A decision
    17	>    function cannot read prose, so the distinction has to become a *value* —
    18	>    the proposal is a `live_content` of `legacy_pristine_partial`, meaning a
    19	>    tree carrying an entry the fingerprint cannot hash. See OQ-7.
    20	>
    21	> The baseline map was measured against the table in this state, so the map and
    22	> the table agree with each other. Reconciling either one is W2 work, after
    23	> ratification.
    24	
    25	## 1. What this document is, and why it exists
    26	
    27	`ADR-155-AMEND-1` decided that framework ownership of the three
    28	**conditional** surfaces — root `PROTOCOL.md`, the `SPEC/v1` contract tree,
    29	and the `.claude/.framework-version` marker — derives from the **registered
    30	delivery record**, never from the ceremony alone and never from file
    31	presence.
    32	
    33	The decision was right. Its *realization* was a cascade of `if` branches
    34	spread across `scripts/install.sh`, `scripts/upgrade.sh` and
    35	`scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh`. That shape has a measured failure
    36	mode: over eleven consecutive cross-model review rounds on the same code,
    37	**35 distinct defects** were reported, and roughly half of the later ones
    38	were regressions introduced by the fix for the round immediately before.
    39	The 45-check end-to-end suite stayed green throughout — it exercises eight
    40	scenarios, and the decision space is a nine-dimensional product.
    41	
    42	The cause is not carelessness. It is that **"correct" was being decided one
    43	branch at a time**, so two branches could encode contradictory answers to
    44	the same question and nothing would notice. This document makes the space
    45	explicit so that contradictions surface *before* they become defects.
    46	
    47	Division of labour, strictly observed:
    48	
    49	| Artifact | Role |
    50	|---|---|
    51	| this document | defines the dimensions, the legality rules, and the reasoning |
    52	| `scripts/tests/ownership_table.tsv` | **the truth** — one row per legal cell, with its expected verdict |
    53	| `scripts/tests/test-ownership-table.sh` | executes every row against the **real** scripts |
    54	
    55	**No value is duplicated between this document and the TSV.** If you want to
    56	know what a given cell decides, read the TSV. If you want to know *why the
    57	cell exists at all*, read this.
    58	
    59	## 2. The nine dimensions
    60	
    61	A "cell" is one assignment of all nine. The subject under test is one
    62	surface's outcome on one run.
    63	
    64	### 2.1 `surface`
    65	
    66	| Value | Path | Shape |
    67	|---|---|---|
    68	| `spec` | `SPEC/v1` | a **tree** |
    69	| `protocol` | root `PROTOCOL.md` | a **generated pointer** — no source file; the body is a heredoc built from `$SOURCE_DIR`/`$TARGET`/`$PROFILE`/`$STACK` |
    70	| `marker` | `.claude/.framework-version` | a tracked single-line file |
    71	
    72	The three differ in more than their path, and every difference has produced
    73	at least one defect. `spec` is the only tree (so it is the only surface with
    74	descendants, per-file records, and a "partially populated" state);
    75	`protocol` is the only surface with no bytes in the source (so `source_has`
    76	is meaningless for it, and its baseline digest comes from a *computed*
    77	canonical hash); `marker` is the only surface inside `.claude/`, so it is
    78	the only one both ceremonies receive.
    79	
    80	### 2.2 `prior_record` — what the PRE-run baseline manifest says
    81	
    82	| Value | Meaning |
    83	|---|---|
    84	| `none` | no record line for this relpath |
    85	| `hash` | a `<64-hex>  <relpath>` record |
    86	| `link_match` | a `LINK  <relpath>  <target>` record whose target equals the live `readlink` |
    87	| `link_retargeted` | a `LINK` record whose target does **not** equal the live `readlink` |
    88	
    89	This dimension describes the **previous** run's testimony, read before
    90	anything is written this run. It is the operative meaning of "registered
